WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.220
NAEP is called The Nation's Report Card
because these test scores consistently

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.450
measure student learning over time. 2019's results were just released, and

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.090
warrant three takeaways and a caution. First,
results were grim. Math scores were up a

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.660
tick in fourth grade, but they dropped in
eighth grade, and both grades dropped in

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.500
reading. Indeed, eighth grade reading
scores changed more than at any time in

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.429
that test's history, and in the wrong
direction. Second, these declines look

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:33.390
worse against the backdrop of the past
decade. While NAEP scores mostly climbed

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:38.399
from 1990 through 2010, performance
stagnated since, and 2015 saw widespread

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:43.680
declines for the first time — until now.
Third, declines were driven by our lowest

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.219
scoring students, and since high
performing students stayed flat, the gap

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:51.930
between them is growing. A caution: After
this lousy report card, expect to see a

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.469
number of articles offering pet
explanations for the poor showing. Truth

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:59.340
is, there are simply too many factors
involved to know exactly why scores

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:04.199
declined, but even if they can't pinpoint
a cause, these results are a sobering

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.840
reminder of where our students are.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.360
Are you more concerned with the declines on

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.830
NAEP, or on the growing divide between
low- and high-performing students? Let us

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.939
know in our poll. Also, let us know what
other topics you'd like our scholars to

00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:22.110
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like
and subscribe for more research and

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.490
videos from AEI.

